{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "050S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$W$", "MATH_0004": "$W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to W$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-check-quasi-compact-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87955b6b44be14f27ae02579c55634c9110a1b1232924689b9913f16226d9a28", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49accd0d4738ff584c143d6787c3b4feaed2f6c8af4dfb4afc4b896b75009040", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be surjective, flat, and locally of finite\npresentation where <MATH_0003> is an algebraic space. If the base change\n<MATH_0004> is quasi-compact, then\n<MATH_0005> is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2ac0078e795f6311126583179519ffaa73362a58708f354b60f5c4337d0e046b", "unit_id": "tag:0DTL:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "050S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to W$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$U' \\subset U$", "MATH_0009": "$U' \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0010": "$U' \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} =\nU' \\times_W (W \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X})$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b8416ecb94924fa5afa8577b64f60e101269cc3a177701b201aecb5da18ac0b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d9fb292ef6675aa9173b624a0f4ace2c5094273227c2af9aebc96ec58125c938", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism with <MATH_0003>\na quasi-compact algebraic stack. Choose a scheme <MATH_0004> and a surjective\nsmooth morphism\n<MATH_0005>.\nSince <MATH_0006> is flat, surjective, and locally of finite\npresentation and <MATH_0007> is quasi-compact, we can find a\nquasi-compact open subscheme <MATH_0008> such that\n<MATH_0009> is surjective.\nThen\n<MATH_0010>\nis quasi-compact by assumption and surjects onto\n<MATH_0011>.\nHence <MATH_0012>\nis quasi-compact as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:55cd585de1ddf8821cc38c4c7950eef1f36d02da3f8b44c8afaf74126b32829c", "unit_id": "tag:0DTL:proof"}
